  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "If $a>0, b>0$ then the maximum area of the parallelogram whose three vertices are $O(0,0), A(a \\cos \\theta, b \\sin \\theta)$ and $\\mathrm{B}(\\mathrm{a} \\cos \\theta,-\\mathrm{b} \\sin \\theta)$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "KPFeg",
      "text": "ab when $\\theta=\\pi / 4$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "0fln8",
      "text": "3 ab when $\\theta=\\pi / 4$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "f7VpK",
      "text": "ab when $\\theta=\\pi / 2$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "3msvr",
      "text": "$2 \\mathrm{ab}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Area $\\mathrm{OABC}=2 \\times$ area $\\triangle \\mathrm{OAB}$\r\n$\\begin{array}{l}\r\n=2 \\times\\left(\\frac{1}{2} \\times \\mathrm{OM} \\times \\mathrm{AB}\\right) \\\\\r\n=2 \\times \\frac{1}{2}|\\mathrm{a} \\cos \\theta \\times 2 \\mathrm{~b} \\sin \\theta|=2 \\times \\mathrm{ab}|\\sin \\theta \\cos \\theta| \\\\\r\n=\\mathrm{ab}|\\sin 2 \\theta|\r\n\\end{array}$\r\n$\\therefore$ Maximum is ab when $\\theta=\\pi / 4$\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/73FBTtrTPxi888I5kAlL5eo6NlfoBoWIg1O2jJuh4gg.original.fullsize.png\">",
